WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.227 --> 00:00:09.761
appears to be in the final

00:00:09.895 --> 00:00:10.963
stretch of his investigations

00:00:11.096 --> 00:00:13.031
into former president Donald

00:00:13.165 --> 00:00:13.599
Trump.

00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:14.800
Smith has been looking into the

00:00:14.933 --> 00:00:16.501
possible mishandling of

00:00:16.635 --> 00:00:17.603
classified documents and efforts

00:00:17.669 --> 00:00:20.372
to obstruct the 2020 election.

00:00:20.505 --> 00:00:23.108
Now notable development this

00:00:23.242 --> 00:00:25.277
week, Tim parlatore, one of

00:00:25.611 --> 00:00:28.013
trump's key attorneys, announced

00:00:28.146 --> 00:00:30.115
he is leaving the team.

00:00:30.249 --> 00:00:31.116
He worked on January 6th

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.184
investigation and played a key

00:00:32.317 --> 00:00:33.952
role in the mar-a-lago documents

00:00:34.086 --> 00:00:35.954
probe, including organizing

00:00:36.088 --> 00:00:37.623
additional searches at trump

00:00:37.656 --> 00:00:39.258
tower, bedminster and an office

00:00:39.625 --> 00:00:40.592
in palm beach as well as a

00:00:40.726 --> 00:00:42.394
Florida storage unit.

00:00:42.527 --> 00:00:43.996
Parlatore also appeared before

00:00:44.129 --> 00:00:46.531
the grand jury for several hours

00:00:46.665 --> 00:00:48.467
back in December and Tim joins

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.635
me now.

00:00:49.735 --> 00:00:50.802
Tim, thanks so much for being

00:00:50.936 --> 00:00:51.637
here with us.

00:00:51.637 --> 00:00:52.871
I think everybody wants to know

00:00:53.005 --> 00:00:54.840
after the news this week, why

00:00:54.973 --> 00:00:56.575
did you leave the former

00:00:56.708 --> 00:00:57.643
president's legal team?

00:00:57.776 --> 00:01:00.812
&gt;&gt; So, as I said at the time, it

00:01:00.946 --> 00:01:02.347
had nothing to do with the case

00:01:02.481 --> 00:01:03.649
or the client.

00:01:03.682 --> 00:01:05.884
The real reason is because there

00:01:06.018 --> 00:01:06.585
are certain individuals that

00:01:06.718 --> 00:01:08.787
made defending the president

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:09.721
much harder than it needed to

00:01:09.855 --> 00:01:09.988
be.

00:01:10.122 --> 00:01:11.690
In particular, there is one

00:01:11.823 --> 00:01:14.426
individual who works for him,

00:01:14.559 --> 00:01:16.161
Boris Epstein, who had really

00:01:16.295 --> 00:01:17.963
done everything he could to try

00:01:18.096 --> 00:01:21.033
to block us, to prevent us from

00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:23.268
doing what we could to defend

00:01:23.669 --> 00:01:25.304
the president, and ultimately it

00:01:25.671 --> 00:01:26.972
got to a point where it's

00:01:27.105 --> 00:01:28.206
difficult enough fighting

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.677
against doj and in this case

00:01:31.677 --> 00:01:32.144
special counsel, but when you

00:01:32.277 --> 00:01:33.679
have people within the tent that

00:01:33.679 --> 00:01:34.813
are also trying to undermine

00:01:34.946 --> 00:01:38.183
you, block you, and really make

00:01:38.317 --> 00:01:40.686
it so that I can't do what I

00:01:40.819 --> 00:01:44.423
know that I need to do as a

00:01:44.556 --> 00:01:46.358
lawyer and when I am getting

00:01:46.491 --> 00:01:48.960
into fights like that, that's

00:01:49.094 --> 00:01:49.828
detracting from what is

00:01:49.961 --> 00:01:50.996
necessary to defend the client

00:01:51.129 --> 00:01:53.699
and ultimately was not in the

00:01:53.699 --> 00:01:54.066
client's best interest.

00:01:54.199 --> 00:01:55.701
So I made the decision to

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:55.934
withdraw.

00:01:56.068 --> 00:01:58.103
&gt;&gt; Infighting is nothing new in

00:01:58.236 --> 00:01:58.537
trump world.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.172
Is there any specific incidents

00:02:00.305 --> 00:02:02.240
of something a he did to, as you

00:02:02.374 --> 00:02:03.975
say, prevent you from being able

00:02:04.109 --> 00:02:05.177
to properly represent your

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:05.711
client?

00:02:05.711 --> 00:02:06.411
&gt;&gt; Sure.

00:02:07.813 --> 00:02:10.215
I mean, he served as kind of a

00:02:10.349 --> 00:02:12.784
filter to present us from getting

00:02:12.918 --> 00:02:14.052
information to client, getting

00:02:14.186 --> 00:02:15.954
information from the client.

00:02:16.088 --> 00:02:17.389
In my opinion, he was not very

00:02:17.723 --> 00:02:18.824
honest with us or with the

00:02:18.957 --> 00:02:20.392
client on certain things.

00:02:20.525 --> 00:02:21.293
There were certain things like

00:02:21.727 --> 00:02:23.161
the searches that he had

00:02:23.295 --> 00:02:25.731
attempted to interfere with, and

00:02:25.797 --> 00:02:27.032
then more recently, as we're

00:02:27.165 --> 00:02:29.735
coming down to the end of this

00:02:29.768 --> 00:02:31.737
investigation where jack Smith

00:02:31.803 --> 00:02:32.504
and ultimately Merrick Garland

00:02:32.637 --> 00:02:35.407
is going to make a decision as

00:02:35.741 --> 00:02:37.909
to what to do, we put together

00:02:38.043 --> 00:02:40.846
our defense strategy to educate

00:02:40.979 --> 00:02:41.747
Merrick Garland as to how best

00:02:41.847 --> 00:02:44.349
to handle this matter, he was

00:02:44.483 --> 00:02:46.284
preventing us from engaging in

00:02:46.418 --> 00:02:46.752
that strategy.

00:02:46.885 --> 00:02:47.919
&gt;&gt; You said that Boris tried to

00:02:48.053 --> 00:02:49.755
prevent you from conducting

00:02:49.755 --> 00:02:49.855
searches.

00:02:49.988 --> 00:02:50.822
What searches?

00:02:50.956 --> 00:02:55.761
&gt;&gt; The search at bedminster

00:02:55.827 --> 00:02:56.061
initially.

00:02:56.194 --> 00:02:56.895
There was a lot of pushback from

00:02:57.028 --> 00:02:57.162
him.

00:02:57.295 --> 00:02:58.864
He didn't want us doing the

00:02:58.997 --> 00:02:59.765
search.

00:02:59.765 --> 00:03:00.365
And we had eventually overcome

00:03:00.499 --> 00:03:02.334
him.

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:03.902
&gt;&gt; Why didn't he want you doing

00:03:04.035 --> 00:03:04.569
the search?

00:03:04.703 --> 00:03:05.070
&gt;&gt; I don't know.

00:03:05.203 --> 00:03:08.106
You know, Boris is -- you know,

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:09.408
he is a lawyer.

00:03:09.775 --> 00:03:11.777
He spent about 18 months at a

00:03:11.777 --> 00:03:13.011
big firm doing transactional

00:03:13.145 --> 00:03:15.113
work and I think he thinks based

00:03:15.247 --> 00:03:17.215
on that experience he knows

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:19.251
better than us.

00:03:19.384 --> 00:03:19.918
&gt;&gt; You previously testified

00:03:20.051 --> 00:03:22.254
before the grand jury in

00:03:22.387 --> 00:03:22.621
December.

00:03:22.754 --> 00:03:25.791
Some people speculated you

00:03:25.791 --> 00:03:26.858
couldn't represent the former

00:03:26.992 --> 00:03:27.793
president because you're a

00:03:27.793 --> 00:03:27.993
witness.

00:03:28.126 --> 00:03:29.828
What is your response?

00:03:29.961 --> 00:03:31.296
&gt;&gt; That unfortunately is a lack

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:31.863
of understanding.

00:03:31.997 --> 00:03:33.799
First of all, I was not

00:03:33.799 --> 00:03:34.032
subpoenaed.

00:03:34.166 --> 00:03:35.801
What that was so the original

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:39.004
subpoena to the office of the

00:03:39.137 --> 00:03:40.472
former president, they wanted a

00:03:40.605 --> 00:03:41.840
custodian of records to appear.

00:03:41.973 --> 00:03:44.176
They really wanted is a staffer

00:03:44.309 --> 00:03:45.811
from palm beach to talk about,

00:03:45.844 --> 00:03:46.878
you know, what searches were

00:03:47.012 --> 00:03:49.281
done so they could beat them up,

00:03:49.414 --> 00:03:50.348
and ultimately there wasn't

00:03:50.482 --> 00:03:52.818
really a good person on the

00:03:52.951 --> 00:03:53.251
staff to send.

00:03:53.385 --> 00:03:54.386
So we made the decision, I made

00:03:54.519 --> 00:03:57.122
the decision to go in myself and

00:03:57.255 --> 00:04:00.025
to face the prosecutors and to

00:04:00.158 --> 00:04:00.926
actually speak directly to the

00:04:01.059 --> 00:04:02.527
grand jury and explain them what

00:04:02.661 --> 00:04:05.063
was really going on here.

00:04:05.197 --> 00:04:06.798
So as I went in and I talked

00:04:06.932 --> 00:04:08.867
about what we, as a legal team,

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.936
had done in searching all the

00:04:11.069 --> 00:04:13.472
properties, that doesn't make me

00:04:13.839 --> 00:04:14.372
a material witness or anything

00:04:14.506 --> 00:04:15.841
like that.

00:04:15.874 --> 00:04:19.110
So there is no conflict.

00:04:19.244 --> 00:04:20.078
There is no issue or -- I would

00:04:20.212 --> 00:04:21.847
expect to ever be called back in

00:04:21.847 --> 00:04:21.913
there.

00:04:22.047 --> 00:04:24.115
In fact, there were a couple of

00:04:24.249 --> 00:04:25.851
opportunities where I offered to

00:04:25.851 --> 00:04:25.917
come back.

00:04:26.051 --> 00:04:27.886
The prosecutors didn't want me

00:04:28.019 --> 00:04:28.286
back.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:30.655
So it really has nothing to do

00:04:30.789 --> 00:04:31.056
with that.

00:04:31.189 --> 00:04:32.390
&gt;&gt; So you recently sent a letter

00:04:32.524 --> 00:04:34.292
with the other attorneys on the

00:04:34.426 --> 00:04:36.461
legal team to the house

00:04:36.595 --> 00:04:38.129
select -- the house permanent

00:04:38.263 --> 00:04:39.431
select committee on

00:04:39.865 --> 00:04:39.998
intelligence.

00:04:39.998 --> 00:04:40.198
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:04:40.332 --> 00:04:40.932
&gt;&gt; One of the arguments you make

00:04:41.066 --> 00:04:42.467
is the reason the documents

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:43.869
enended up in mar-a-lago because

00:04:43.869 --> 00:04:46.304
at the end of any

00:04:46.438 --> 00:04:47.005
administration, particularly

00:04:47.138 --> 00:04:48.173
this one, it's chaotic and

00:04:48.306 --> 00:04:49.875
specifically you said that the

00:04:50.008 --> 00:04:51.243
fact that these ended up at

00:04:51.376 --> 00:04:53.111
mar-a-lago is, quote, indicative

00:04:53.245 --> 00:04:55.881
of the staff's packing process

00:04:55.914 --> 00:04:57.883
and not any criminal intent by

00:04:57.883 --> 00:05:02.320
former president trump.

00:05:02.454 --> 00:05:02.988
The problem is, the former

00:05:03.121 --> 00:05:04.222
president and his allies and one

00:05:04.356 --> 00:05:06.424
of your fellow attorneys have

00:05:06.558 --> 00:05:08.727
all publicly contradicted that

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:11.897
explanation for how these things

00:05:11.897 --> 00:05:12.430
ended up down at mar-a-lago.

00:05:12.564 --> 00:05:13.999
At least four official

00:05:14.132 --> 00:05:14.866
explanations that they have put

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.368
down about the status of these

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:16.735
documents.

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:19.504
I want to go through them

00:05:19.905 --> 00:05:19.971
chronologically.

00:05:20.105 --> 00:05:20.605
Starting after the search

00:05:20.739 --> 00:05:21.907
warrant as executed at

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:22.741
mar-a-lago some of the president

00:05:22.874 --> 00:05:24.476
Putin it's Al lace came out and

00:05:24.609 --> 00:05:28.246
said he issued a sweeping

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:28.880
declassification order on

00:05:29.014 --> 00:05:29.915
multiple occasions so that the

00:05:29.915 --> 00:05:31.182
documents removed from the oval

00:05:31.316 --> 00:05:32.684
office were deemed declassified

00:05:32.817 --> 00:05:33.919
when he removed them.

00:05:33.919 --> 00:05:36.288
Did you ever see any evidence of

00:05:36.421 --> 00:05:37.155
any such order?

00:05:37.289 --> 00:05:42.761
&gt;&gt; I never saw the order.

00:05:42.894 --> 00:05:43.428
You know, that would not be

00:05:43.562 --> 00:05:44.229
something that we would have

00:05:44.362 --> 00:05:46.531
access to, if it was a written

00:05:46.665 --> 00:05:48.066
order as opposed to an oral

00:05:48.199 --> 00:05:48.366
order.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:49.935
I didn't see that.

00:05:49.935 --> 00:05:51.937
&gt;&gt; So the former president then

00:05:52.037 --> 00:05:52.904
a couple weeks later said this

00:05:53.038 --> 00:05:57.375
to Sean hannity.

00:05:57.509 --> 00:05:58.343
&gt;&gt; If you are the president of

00:05:58.476 --> 00:06:00.278
the United States, you can

00:06:00.412 --> 00:06:01.413
declassify by saying it's

00:06:01.546 --> 00:06:02.147
declassified, even by thinking

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:03.949
about it.

00:06:03.982 --> 00:06:07.552
&gt;&gt; So the letter says that he

00:06:07.953 --> 00:06:08.553
wasn't really aware of these

00:06:08.687 --> 00:06:09.955
documents being placed because

00:06:09.955 --> 00:06:11.489
it was chaotic, they all were

00:06:11.623 --> 00:06:13.091
shipped to mar-a-lago.

00:06:13.224 --> 00:06:15.260
How can you declassify something

00:06:15.393 --> 00:06:17.963
with your mind if you don't know

00:06:17.963 --> 00:06:20.498
that it's in one of these boxes?

00:06:20.632 --> 00:06:23.535
&gt;&gt; These are two unrelated

00:06:23.969 --> 00:06:24.035
concepts.

00:06:24.035 --> 00:06:25.303
So there is the issue of

00:06:25.437 --> 00:06:27.973
classification or

00:06:27.973 --> 00:06:28.239
declassification.

00:06:28.373 --> 00:06:29.975
That's separate and apart from

00:06:29.975 --> 00:06:31.042
the issue of document management

00:06:31.176 --> 00:06:33.478
and what goes in the boxes.

00:06:33.612 --> 00:06:34.846
One of the things that we were

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:36.848
trying to explain there is that

00:06:36.982 --> 00:06:38.617
the processes that are in play

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:42.520
in the white house, in the oval

00:06:42.654 --> 00:06:43.488
office, they don't match the

00:06:43.622 --> 00:06:45.991
same level of, you know, care,

00:06:46.091 --> 00:06:47.459
if you will, that are done in

00:06:47.592 --> 00:06:48.660
the intelligence agencies and in

00:06:48.793 --> 00:06:49.995
the military.

00:06:49.995 --> 00:06:52.564
And so marked documents, whether

00:06:52.697 --> 00:06:54.199
classified or key classified,

00:06:54.332 --> 00:06:56.968
and unclassified documents get

00:06:57.102 --> 00:06:57.335
mixed in.

00:06:57.469 --> 00:06:58.103
This is not just about when

00:06:58.236 --> 00:06:59.170
packed up to leave.

00:06:59.304 --> 00:07:00.972
This is about the four years

00:07:01.106 --> 00:07:03.141
while they are in office.

00:07:03.274 --> 00:07:04.476
Now, since we submitted this

00:07:04.609 --> 00:07:06.611
letter we found out that the

00:07:06.745 --> 00:07:10.015
archivist testified that every

00:07:10.015 --> 00:07:10.515
administration going back to

00:07:10.649 --> 00:07:11.616
Reagan has had the exact same

00:07:12.017 --> 00:07:12.050
issue.

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:13.652
That's what we were talking

00:07:14.019 --> 00:07:14.052
about there.

00:07:14.185 --> 00:07:16.888
So the procedures for

00:07:17.022 --> 00:07:18.023
declassification is a separate

00:07:18.023 --> 00:07:20.025
issue from how these boxes were

00:07:20.025 --> 00:07:22.160
packed and how the documents

00:07:22.293 --> 00:07:24.763
were kept during that four

00:07:24.896 --> 00:07:25.063
years.

00:07:25.196 --> 00:07:25.697
&gt;&gt; Now, we know from CNN

00:07:26.031 --> 00:07:26.865
reporting this week jack Smith,

00:07:26.998 --> 00:07:28.133
the special counsel, is

00:07:28.266 --> 00:07:32.037
interested in this process and

00:07:32.037 --> 00:07:32.537
especially how much your former

00:07:32.671 --> 00:07:34.072
client knew and understood about

00:07:34.205 --> 00:07:34.572
the process.

00:07:35.006 --> 00:07:36.775
A fellow attorney who signed

00:07:36.908 --> 00:07:38.043
this letter told Erin Burnett

00:07:38.043 --> 00:07:40.045
earlier this week.

00:07:40.178 --> 00:07:43.381
&gt;&gt; He is aware of a bureaucratic

00:07:43.515 --> 00:07:45.316
process that can be used.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:48.053
At the end of his presidency he

00:07:48.053 --> 00:07:48.620
relied on constitutional

00:07:48.753 --> 00:07:50.055
authority as commander-in-chief

00:07:50.088 --> 00:07:51.456
which is to take documents and

00:07:51.589 --> 00:07:53.491
take them to mar-a-lago while

00:07:53.625 --> 00:07:55.260
still president as we was at the

00:07:55.393 --> 00:07:58.063
time and to effectively

00:07:58.063 --> 00:07:58.963
declassify and personalize them.

00:07:59.097 --> 00:08:00.665
He talked about declassifying

00:08:00.799 --> 00:08:02.067
them but he didn't need to.

00:08:02.167 --> 00:08:04.069
&gt;&gt; So it appears that he is

00:08:04.069 --> 00:08:05.670
saying that during the

00:08:06.071 --> 00:08:06.771
presidency former president

00:08:06.905 --> 00:08:09.140
trump followed the process for

00:08:09.274 --> 00:08:10.075
declassifying but towards the

00:08:10.075 --> 00:08:12.944
end of the presidency he did

00:08:13.078 --> 00:08:13.211
not.

00:08:13.344 --> 00:08:14.079
Does that contradict what you

00:08:14.179 --> 00:08:15.580
guys told congress?

00:08:15.714 --> 00:08:16.915
&gt;&gt; It doesn't because again we

00:08:17.048 --> 00:08:18.783
are talking about document

00:08:18.917 --> 00:08:20.385
management, not

00:08:20.518 --> 00:08:20.885
declassification.

00:08:21.019 --> 00:08:22.821
And when it comes to all the

00:08:22.954 --> 00:08:24.089
declassification procedures, one

00:08:24.189 --> 00:08:25.356
thing you have to remember, when

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:28.093
you get a security clearance,

00:08:28.093 --> 00:08:28.893
top secret security clearance,

00:08:29.027 --> 00:08:30.161
you get the training and the

00:08:30.295 --> 00:08:32.630
forms that you have to fill out

00:08:32.764 --> 00:08:35.233
and agreements to sign.

00:08:35.366 --> 00:08:36.601
Presidents don't get that.

00:08:36.735 --> 00:08:38.103
Elected officials, they don't

00:08:38.103 --> 00:08:38.837
have security clearances.

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:40.505
They gain access to this

00:08:40.638 --> 00:08:43.441
material simply by virtue of the

00:08:43.575 --> 00:08:44.109
fact that they were elected.

00:08:44.242 --> 00:08:45.310
So when you're the president,

00:08:45.443 --> 00:08:46.578
you are not actually going in

00:08:46.711 --> 00:08:48.146
the log book and doing the

00:08:48.279 --> 00:08:50.582
entries to declassify something.

00:08:50.715 --> 00:08:51.750
You're just saying to your

00:08:52.117 --> 00:08:53.251
staff, hey, this document here,

00:08:53.718 --> 00:08:54.619
I want declassified.

00:08:54.753 --> 00:08:57.122
Then you kinda take it with you.

00:08:57.255 --> 00:08:58.823
Now, should the staff have

00:08:58.957 --> 00:09:00.925
followed certain procedures?

00:09:01.059 --> 00:09:01.259
Sure.

